        "created_at": "2018-03-06T16:07:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Escher\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/escher/48/4865_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Escher:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div>(Okay, is there any way we can get Absolute Zero to be a polar bear?)</div>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Best I can think of is Absolursus Zero, but that's bears in general rather than polar bears. Maybe something with \"arctic\" as the Greek word <em>arktos </em>actually means \"bear\" (the association is due to the bear constellations)?</p>",
